igation\""]},{"id":"argument_driven","score":0.18,"confidence":"low","evidence":["catalog text contains \"theory\""]},{"id":"narrative","score":0.18,"confidence":"low","evidence":["catalog text contains \"murder\""]}],"method":"deterministic_catalog_heuristics_v1"},"experimentalSemanticProfile":{"centralFigures":[{"name":"Lee Harvey Oswald","confidence":0.98},{"name":"John F. Kennedy","confidence":0.98}],"centralPlaces":[],"argument":{"present":true,"statement":"The evidence shows that conspiracy theories about President Kennedy’s assassination are fraudulent and that Lee Harvey Oswald was responsible for the murder.","confidence":0.94},"academicOrientation":{"score":28,"confidence":0.9},"profileConfidence":0.95,"model":"gpt-5.6-luna","promptVersion":8,"inputHash":"22259b15fed810c3fcb0be6455bd3629c513378de9f678c774439808b5f325c5","reviewStatus":"unreviewed","validationWarnings":[]},"summary":"Polls reveal that over 75 percent of Americans believe there was a conspiracy behind Lee Harvey Oswald; some even believe Oswald was entirely innocent. In this absorbing and historic book--the first ever to cover the entire case--Vincent Bugliosi shows how we have come to believe such lies about an event that changed the course of history. Bugliosi is perhaps the only man in America capable of \"prosecuting\" Oswald for the murder of President Kennedy. His book is a narrative compendium of fact, forensic evidence, reexamination of key witnesses, and common sense. Every detail and nuance is accounted for, every conspiracy theory revealed as a fraud upon the American public. Bugliosi's irresistible logic, command of the evidence, and ability to draw startling inferences shed fresh light on this American nightmare. At last we know what really happened. At last it all makes sense.--From publisher description.","publicationYear":2007,"subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Assassination","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-reclaimin